source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: Jira resolves no dangerous scheme and renders an error span; jiro keeps the target and its title reversible in the link directive.
-- input.jira --
[x|javascript:alert(1)|t]
-- rendered.html --
<p><span class="error">&#91;x|javascript:alert(1)|t&#93;</span></p>
-- want.md --
:link[x]{target="javascript:alert(1)" title="t"}
-- warnings.json --
[
 {
  "Line": 1,
  "Column": 1,
  "Construct": "link",
  "Reason": "dangerous destination scheme requires a reversible link directive"
 }
]
